        "url": "https://9to5mac.com/2026/06/01/controller-for-homekit-app-adds-ai-feature-just-say-it/",
        "content_text": "<div class=\"feat-image\"><img src=\"https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/06/Controller-for-HomeKit-app-adds-AI-feature-Just-say-it.jpg?quality=82&#038;strip=all&#038;w=1600\" /></div><p>The Controller for HomeKit app has just been updated with a new AI feature which the developer is promoting with the phrase “just say it”. </p>\n\n\n\n<p>The idea is that you use natural language to describe what you want to happen and the AI will automatically create the required <a href=\"https://9to5mac.com/guides/homekit/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">HomeKit</a> scene, workflow, and/or automation … </p>\n\n\n\n <a data-layer-pagetype=\"post\" data-layer-postcategory=\"homekit\" data-layer-viewtype=\"unknown\" data-post-id=\"1053989\" href=\"https://9to5mac.com/2026/06/01/controller-for-homekit-app-adds-ai-feature-just-say-it/#more-1053989\" class=\"more-link\">more…</a>",
        "type": "Technology",
