        "content_text": "<div class=\"feat-image\"><img src=\"https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2024/11/carplay-ai-ios181.jpg?quality=82&#038;strip=all&#038;w=1600\" /></div><p>Rivian’s chief software officer, Wassym Bensaid, joined Nilay Patel in the <a href=\"https://www.theverge.com/podcast/929940/rivian-wassym-bensaid-software-volkswagen-carplay-assistant-ai\">latest <em>Decoder</em> interview</a>. And his comments on CarPlay show Rivian continuing to double down on its refusal to support Apple’s platform.</p>\n\n\n\n <a data-layer-pagetype=\"post\" data-layer-postcategory=\"carplay,rivian\" data-layer-viewtype=\"unknown\" data-post-id=\"1053695\" href=\"https://9to5mac.com/2026/05/28/rivian-says-ai-makes-debate-over-carplay-completely-obsolete/#more-1053695\" class=\"more-link\">more…</a>",
